  "id": "COMPOUND:11817 - PROTEIN:46",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Selisistat and von Willebrand factor through a series of molecular interactions. Selisistat is implicated in targeting Calnexin, which is a target of both Antihemophilic factor, human recombinant and Besilesomab. The latter, in turn, has a target of von Willebrand factor, while Selisistat also targets a 78 kDa glucose-regulated protein, which is also a target of Antihemophilic factor, human recombinant. These pathways collectively indicate that Selisistat may influence the von Willebrand factor pathway through its interaction with Calnexin and other proteins in the hemostatic system. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent pattern of interaction, though the strength of the relationship varies slightly across the different pathways. The evidence supports a possible mechanism by which Selisistat could modulate von Willebrand factor, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Selisistat in this specific pathway.",
